---
title: Roast beef sandwich
tags: [beef]
source: The Beef by StarChefs, https://www.starchefs.com/recipes/the-beef
---

> A restaurant batch: the aïoli uses 3.5 kg of mayonnaise. Scale it down.

== Marinated onions ==

Mix the @onions{500%g}(julienned), @parsley{50%g}(chopped), @basil{}(chopped),
@oregano{}(fresh, chopped) and @pomegranate molasses{12%oz}. Cover and
refrigerate ~{2%hours}.

== Peppercorn aïoli ==

Boil the @veal stock{16%cups} in a #stockpot{} over medium heat until it
coats a spoon and only 4 cups remain. Keep it warm.

Heat some @neutral oil{} in a #saucepan{} over low heat and cook the
@onions{2.4%kg}(julienned) until caramelized.

Blend the onions in a #blender{} with the @red wine vinegar{330%g},
@black peppercorns{300%g}(ground) and the reduced stock until smooth. Let it
cool.

Whisk in the @mayonnaise{3.5%kg}(Japanese-style) and @kosher salt{100%g}.

== Sandwich ==

Spread the aïoli on both cut sides of a @baguette{}(toasted, split).

On the bottom half, stack the @potato sticks{}(fried), @roast beef{}(sliced),
@cheddar cheese{}(sharp white) and the marinated onions. Close and serve.
